---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Glyph from "../components/Glyph.astro";
import { getAllTools, REPO_URL } from "../lib/tools";

const tools = getAllTools();
const description =
  "What ohmyharness is, how facts are checked, the neutrality policy, and how to add or correct a tool.";

const legend = [
  { value: true, label: "Confirmed" },
  { value: false, label: "Confirmed absent" },
  { value: null, label: "Not verified yet" },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={description} path="/about">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">A directory you can check.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        ohmyharness lists the runtimes that run coding agents and the apps that
        orchestrate them. It is open source, community maintained, and built so
        that every claim can be traced to a source.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What this is</h2>
        <p>
          There are dozens of AI coding tools now, and the categories are easy
          to mix up. A <strong>harness</strong> is the runtime that talks to a
          model and runs tools. An <strong>orchestrator</strong> is an app that
          runs one or more harnesses. A <strong>cloud agent</strong> works in a
          hosted sandbox and hands back a pull request. An
          <strong>add-on</strong> is a plugin or distribution that extends one
          harness or orchestrator.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each tool has one page with the facts that matter when you choose:
          who makes it, what it runs on, how you pay for it, and which features
          are confirmed. The same facts power the comparison matrix and the
          tier-list maker.
        </p>

        <h2 id="legend">How to read a tool page</h2>
        <p>
          Features have three states, and the third one is the important one:
        </p>
        <div class="legend-row" style="justify-content:flex-start;gap:18px;margin-block:4px">
          {legend.map((item) => (
            <span class="legend"><Glyph value={item.value} label={item.label} /> {item.label}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p>
          <strong>?</strong> means nobody has checked yet. It is not a polite
          way of saying no. We write <strong>✗</strong> only when a source
          confirms a feature is missing, and every page lists the sources used
          for that entry.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pricing and platform facts change often. Each entry carries a
          <strong>last verified</strong> date, and GitHub star counts carry
          their own check date.
        </p>

        <h2>Neutrality</h2>
        <p>
          There are no paid rankings, sponsored placements or affiliate links.
          Order in the directory is alphabetical, tier lists belong to the
          people who make them, and no tool can buy a better position.
        </p>
        <p>
          Taglines describe what a tool does, not how good it is. Comparisons
          show the same rows for every tool so the format cannot favour one
          entry.
        </p>
        <p>
          If the project ever accepts sponsorship, it will be labelled clearly
          and kept away from rankings and comparisons.
        </p>

        <h2>Who makes this</h2>
        <p>
          ohmyharness is maintained by{" "}
          <a href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener">gulivan and contributors</a>.
          The code and the data are MIT licensed. Corrections from tool makers
          and users are equally welcome.
        </p>

        <h2>Data and reuse</h2>
        <p>
          The full dataset is published as JSON at{" "}
          <a href="/api/tools.json">/api/tools.json</a>. Agents and scripts can
          start from <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>. Reuse it under the MIT
          licence; a link back is appreciated.
        </p>
        <p>
          Logos and product names belong to their respective owners and are
          used to identify the products.
        </p>

        <h2>Credits</h2>
        <p>
          The hero animation and logo marquee use components from{" "}
          <a href="https://reactbits.dev" rel="noopener">React Bits</a> by David
          Haz, MIT licensed with a Commons Clause (the components are not
          resold), copied into this repository. Their licence notice is kept
          with the component sources.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="stack">
        <section class="panel">
          <div class="panel__head"><span>Add a tool</span><span>3 steps</span></div>
          <div class="panel__body">
            <div class="step-list">
              <div class="step">
                <span class="step__num">01</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Check the facts</h3>
                  <p>
                    Find a source for each field: the tool's site, docs or
                    repository. If you cannot confirm something, leave it
                    <code>null</code>.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="step">
                <span class="step__num">02</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Add one file</h3>
                  <p>
                    Copy an existing entry in <code>data/tools/</code> to
                    <code>&lt;slug&gt;.json</code> and fill it in. The slug must
                    match the filename.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="step">
                <span class="step__num">03</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>Open a pull request</h3>
                  <p>
                    Checks validate every field. A maintainer reviews the
                    sources, then the tool appears on the site.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="panel">
          <div class="panel__head"><span>Take part</span></div>
          <div class="panel__body stack">
            <div class="edit-links">
              <a class="btn btn--small btn--primary" href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new?template=add-tool.yml`} rel="noopener">Suggest a tool ↗</a>
              <a class="btn btn--small" href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new?template=fix-data.yml`} rel="noopener">Fix a fact ↗</a>
              <a class="btn btn--small btn--ghost" href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`} rel="noopener">Contribution guide ↗</a>
            </div>
            <p class="inline-note">
              {tools.length} tools are listed today. The repo also has the
              schema, the site code and the test fixtures.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="panel">
          <div class="panel__head"><span>Open data</span></div>
          <div class="panel__body stack">
            <ul class="sources">
              <li><a href="/api/tools.json">/api/tools.json — every tool</a></li>
              <li><a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt — index for agents</a></li>
              <li><a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`} rel="noopener">MIT licence</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
